read
Usage: read [-r] [-p PROMPT] NAME...

Read a line from stdin into NAME.

Shell builtin. Splits on whitespace if given several names; the last
one absorbs the remainder.

	-r	do not treat backslash as an escape (almost always what you want)
	-p	print PROMPT first

	read -r line < /etc/hostname
	printf 'name? '; read -r answer

See also: echo, printf
